+**Learning Rate Decay for UV Volume Variant [S2]**:
+The learning rates for UV volumes and NTS decay exponentially over epochs:
+$$ l_{uv} = 1 \times 10^{-3} \gamma_{250}^{\text{epoch}} $$
+$$ l_{nts} = 5 \times 10^{-4} \gamma_{1000}^{\text{epoch}} $$
+Where $\gamma = 1 \times 10^{-1}$ is the decay rate. Note: The sources specify different base epochs for the decay start or normalization ($250$ vs $1000$) in the exponents, implying a piecewise or distinct decay schedule for each branch [S2].
 
 ### Parameters
-*   **Learning Rate Decay:** Exponential decay is applied across stages [S1]. For UV Volume variants, decay rates $\gamma = 1 \times 10^{-1}$ are used [S2].
-*   **Loss Weights:** $\lambda_A, \lambda_N, \lambda_D, \lambda_L, \lambda_{visible}, \lambda_{reg}, \lambda_{rerender}$ balance the multi-task loss [S1].
-*   **Ray Sampling:** 64 points sampled along each camera ray between near and far bounds [S2].
-*   **Optimizer:** Adam optimizer [S2].
-*   **Scene Bounds:** Estimated based on the SMPL model [S2].
